{"stage": "review", "action": "scientific_findings", "result": {"verdict": "revise", "findings": ["The lesson's own test 'Identity Q and K with scaling on gives uniform weights' is wrong: with Q=K=[[1,0],[0,1]], raw scores are [[1,0],[0,1]], scaled by sqrt(2) gives [[0.707,0],[0,0.707]], so softmax rows are [0.6698,0.3302] and [0.3302,0.6698], not 0.5. The test expectation (and the exploration 'Equal scores produce uniform attention' which uses K=[[1,0],[1,0]] correctly) must be corrected; the identity-matrix case does NOT give uniform weights.", "The lesson's test 'Scaling off with large scores gives near one-hot weights' expects metrics.2.value (max attention weight) = 100, but max attention weight is a softmax output bounded in [0,1]; the expected value 100 is dimensionally impossible. The correct expectation is 1 (the near-one-hot max weight), and metrics.3.value (min weight) is ~3.72e-44, not 1.", "The exploration 'Scaling controls how sharply attention focuses' uses Q=[[3,0]], K=[[3,0],[0,3]] with scaled:false. Raw scores are [9,0], softmax gives [0.99988, 0.00012] — the first weight is near 1, consistent with the observe text. However, the exploration's stated prediction/observe is fine; the material issue is that the lesson's tests contradict the compute output, so the tests must be replaced with correct analytic expectations."], "reference_tests": [{"name": "Identity Q,K scaled: softmax of [1/sqrt2, 0]", "state": {"Q": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "K": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "V": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "scaled": true}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.2.value", "formula": "Math.exp(1/Math.sqrt(2))/(Math.exp(1/Math.sqrt(2))+1)", "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "formula": "1/(Math.exp(1/Math.sqrt(2))+1)", "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Scaling off large scores: max weight near 1", "state": {"Q": [[10, 0]], "K": [[10, 0], [0, 10]], "V": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "scaled": false}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.2.value", "formula": "1/(1+Math.exp(-100))", "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "formula": "Math.exp(-100)/(1+Math.exp(-100))", "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Equal keys give uniform weights", "state": {"Q": [[1, 0]], "K": [[1, 0], [1, 0]], "V": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "scaled": true}, "expect": [{"path": "metrics.2.value", "value": 0.5, "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "metrics.3.value", "value": 0.5, "atol": 1e-08}]}, {"name": "Output equals weighted sum of V", "state": {"Q": [[1, 1]], "K": [[1, 0], [0, 1]], "V": [[2, 3], [4, 5]], "scaled": true}, "expect": [{"path": "panels.4.values.0.0", "formula": "0.5*2+0.5*4", "atol": 1e-08}, {"path": "panels.4.values.0.1", "formula": "0.5*3+0.5*5", "atol": 1e-08}]}], "invariants": [{"name": "Each attention weight row sums to 1", "expression": "o.metrics && o.panels && o.panels[3].values.every(r => Math.abs(r.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0) - 1) < 1e-6)"}, {"name": "Output equals weights times V (weighted sum identity)", "expression": "o.panels && o.panels[4].values.every((row,i) => row.every((val,j) => Math.abs(val - o.panels[3].values[i].reduce((a,w,k)=>a+w*s.V[k][j],0)) < 1e-6))"}, {"name": "Attention weights are nonnegative and bounded by 1", "expression": "o.panels && o.panels[3].values.every(r => r.every(w => w >= 0 && w <= 1))"}]}, "elapsed_seconds": 83.023}
